## How to use this template

1. Copy to `~/.claude/agents/<your-verifier-name>.md`
2. Replace placeholders:
   - `<verifier-name>` — short hyphenated name
   - `<domain>` — the specific area (e.g., "schema", "performance", "accessibility")
   - `<stack-skill-N>` — preloaded skill names from `~/.claude/skills/`
   - Sweep items — concrete checks for your domain
   - Severity examples — domain-appropriate
3. Verify skill names exist:
   ```bash
   ls ~/.claude/skills/ | grep -E '^(<skill-1>|<skill-2>)$'
   ```
4. Add to your eval-cases: 3 positive prompts, 3 negative
5. Test with `@-mention` first, then check auto-delegation
